Subject: [PATCH 18/22] sheet route: cut-face carrier conditioning (merge +
 symmetric fans + near-degenerate gate)

Every cut-face carrier node is a crossing of the cut plane with a background grid line, for any orientation (160
random planes, 182587 nodes, 0 off-line), so the cut port has a fixed index set (3267 grid lines). The frozen fan
degenerates when the plane passes near a grid node or a face cut line runs close to a face grid line: aspect ratios
above 1000 in 2.5 % of the c=0 population and 44 % of tilted planes (worst 4e5).

cut_carrier.merge_cut_carrier post-processes the frozen layout (like the Union Jack pass): grid nodes within
eps h = h/10 of the cut have their crossings (and the node itself on a box face) moved to one canonical point on
the plane that also lies on every box face involved, so the trace stays exactly planar, conforming, and identical
between neighbouring cells; every cut-face and clipped polygon is refanned by isometry-invariant rules (lattice
parity square, angle-list anchor, parity quad, exact centroid). Worst aspect ratio after: 22.9 (c=0, 240 cells)
and 18.0 (tilted, 160 planes) on the cut face, 45.6 on box faces; shared-edge audits 400/400 PASS. Two families no
in-face move can fix (plane within eps h of a corner, plane nearly containing an edge) are gated at gap < h/50 with
the GEOMETRY_DEGENERATE receipt and remedy.

Wired into build_carrier_layout (CUT_CARRIER_MERGE), recorded in the receipt and the contract. Tests: aspect bound
and planarity, near-corner gate, uncut untouched, neighbour agreement on a shared face, 48-symmetry invariance.
Four cells labelled end to end through the merged pipeline PASS (rigid residual <= 1.7e-13); an 11-offset sweep
across merge events shows operator steps of 0.9e-3 to 1.2e-3 with and without an event.

